//www.nature.com/articles/s41563-022-01429-5","retrieved":"2026-08-27","title":"Mycorrhizal fungal signaling"},{"id":"naturalis:arbuscular-review","kind":"repository-pdf","locator":"https://repository.naturalis.nl/pub/800999/Verbeek-2025-Arbuscular-mycorrhiza-A.pdf","retrieved":"2026-08-27","title":"Arbuscular mycorrhiza review"}]},"path":"provenance/sources.json"},{"content":{"name":"Fogwood composition data","notice":"Local declarative composition data; source papers retain their own rights.","spdx":"CC0-1.0"},"path":"provenance/license.json"},{"content":"Fogwood keeps this package local, immutable, and reviewable. Source URLs are provenance only.\n","path":"provenance/NOTICE.md"},{"content":{"date":"2026-08-27","evidence_id":"fungi-cities-v2-local","reviewer":"Fogwood local catalog review","status":"fixture-tested","tested_boundary":"Compiler and local proposal seams only; no live provider, browser host, or publication qualification."},"path":"provenance/qualification.json"}],"readme":"# Fungi and cities research world\n\nThis is an immutable `composition.v2` starter for a spacious research surface. Irregular fungal and urban clusters remain native, movable marks; typed arrows separate supports, echoes, and open questions. Observed evidence is labeled as observed, while the city-network comparison is explicitly analogy and not a finding.\n\nThe image portal is a provocation only. If a live image capability is actually available, Codex may create bytes outside Fogwood and bring accepted bytes through the existing `add_materials` proposal path. This package bundles no image and never claims host availability.\n\nStage this composition for page review. Apply and later mutation remain human/page-owned.\n","recipes":[{"content":{"adapters":[{"capability_id":"adapter.materials.v1","id":"adapter:materials","locality":"local","loss":"annotated","purpose":"Bring observed local image bytes through the page proposal bridge when a live capability is observed."},{"capability_